# The fixture models — where they come from and what may be done with them

Two sets live here.

## The five canon-v1 fixtures

`blender.glb`, `blender-interleaved.glb`, `cad.glb`, `cad-split.glb`,
`sketchfab.glb` — one bench written the way three tools write it, made by
`tools/make-asset-fixtures.mjs` for `client/test/canon.test.js`. Their bytes
are pinned by that test: do not re-make them unless canon-v1 changes.

## The twelve foundation models (TASKS-foundation.md FND.0)

`tree-fir.glb`, `tree-larch.glb`, `bush.glb`, `rock.glb`, `street-lamp.glb`,
`billboard.glb`, `bus.glb`, `tunnel-portal.glb`, `bridge-deck.glb`,
`wall-segment-2m.glb`, `kerb-segment-1m.glb`, `pebble-segment-5cm.glb`.

| source | made here, by `tools/make-fixture-models.mjs` (which builds them out of `tools/glbkit.mjs`) |
|---|---|
| licence | **CC0 1.0** — dedicated to the public domain by the splatworld project. No attribution is required, and none of it is anybody else's work. |
| why not downloaded | FND.0 asks for CC0 models. Every CC0 host — Poly Haven, Sketchfab, Kenney, ambientCG — is denied at this container's egress proxy, and a fixture that cannot be re-made on the machine that needs it is not a fixture. |

They are boxes and prisms at real sizes, which is what the stories measure:
a segment's repeat length (`wall-segment-2m` is 2.00 m along X,
`kerb-segment-1m` is 1.00 m), a live part's node name (`head` on the lamp,
`screen` on the billboard), a terrain opening's footprint (`mouth` on the
tunnel portal), and a tree's height for scatter. Re-make them with
`node tools/make-fixture-models.mjs`; the bytes are the same every time.

Replacing any of them with a real model off a CC0 site is welcome on a machine
that can reach one: keep the file name and the node names, put the real
source and licence in the table above, and the stories will not notice.

## The three materials (FND.5)

`asphalt.png`, `kerb-stone.png` and `too-big.png` (3000 px wide on purpose:
story 20 registers it and reads the refusal), made by
`tools/make-fixture-materials.mjs`, deterministic, **CC0 1.0** on the same
terms as the models above.
